# vergeio_snapshot_profile (Resource)

Creates a snapshot profile in VergeOS. A profile is the schedule a VM, volume, or cloud snapshot follows. [`vergeio_vm`](vm.html) stores the profile key in `snapshot_profile`. Cloud snapshots use this same profile. There is no separate cloud snapshot profile. [`vergeio_site_sync_outgoing`](site_sync_outgoing.html) points `period.profile_period` at one of these period keys.

```terraform
snapshot_profile = tonumber(vergeio_snapshot_profile.nightly.id)
```

Each `period` block is one schedule: how often (`frequency`), the time of day (`hour` and `minute`), how long to keep the snapshot (`retention`), and whether the guest is quiesced (`quiesce`). `retention` is seconds. It is required. There is no default. VergeOS expires the snapshot after that many seconds. A missing retention is not keep-forever. Clients that omit the field have stored a 24 hour expiry. Zero is rejected.

`name` is unique within the profile. Changing a period name replaces that period. A period left out of the configuration is deleted. Omit an optional period argument to leave the current value unchanged. An omitted value is not sent.

Destroying the profile deletes its periods. Remove `snapshot_profile` from a VM that still uses the profile, or destroy that VM in the same configuration, before destroying the profile.

